<section id="troubleshooting">
<h3>Troubleshooting</h3>
<p>Open the line that matches what you see.</p>

<h4>Opening the grader</h4>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>There is no Unified Grader item on the activity</summary>
    <div>
        <ul>
            <li>The activity type must be switched on under <a href="#settings-general">General settings</a>. Only assignments are on by default.</li>
            <li>The user must hold <code>local/unifiedgrader:grade</code> in the activity. Non-editing teachers do not have it by default; <code>viewall</code> is not enough.</li>
            <li>Students never see the item.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</details>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>A teacher sees only some students, or cannot post the whole class</summary>
    <div>
        <p>The activity uses separate groups and the teacher does not have <em>Access all groups</em>.
        They see and post their own groups. Check also the group selector in the student list, which
        opens on the teacher's own groups.</p>
    </div>
</details>

<h4>Preview and conversion</h4>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details" id="ts-conversion-port">
    <summary>Conversion fails although the conversion server is up</summary>
    <div>
        <p><strong>What teachers see:</strong> <em>This file could not be converted to PDF for
        preview.</em> with a <strong>Retry conversion</strong> button, and retrying does not help.</p>
        <p><strong>Likely cause:</strong> the converter listens on a non-standard port. Moodle
        sends the file to it, but Moodle's HTTP security then refuses to download the converted
        file from that port. The underlying error is <em>The URL is blocked</em>.</p>
        <p><strong>Fix:</strong> go to <strong>Site administration &gt; General &gt; Security &gt;
        HTTP security</strong> and add the converter's port to the list of allowed ports. Then ask
        the teacher to press <strong>Retry conversion</strong>.</p>
    </div>
</details>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details" id="ts-feedback-pdf-pages">
    <summary>The feedback PDF has the summary but not the student's document, or the marks are missing from its pages</summary>
    <div>
        <p><strong>What students see:</strong> the downloaded PDF stops after the summary page, or
        the document follows but without the highlights, ticks and numbered pins that show on the
        web and the comment cards beside them. The comments are listed in the summary instead.</p>
        <p><strong>Likely cause:</strong> Moodle cannot run Ghostscript. Unified Grader uses it to
        join the document to the summary and to find where each marked phrase sits on the page.</p>
        <p><strong>Fix:</strong> install Ghostscript on the server and set its location under
        <strong>Site administration &gt; Plugins &gt; Activity modules &gt; Assignment &gt; Feedback
        plugins &gt; Annotate PDF</strong> (<em>Ghostscript path</em>). The <em>Test Ghostscript
        path</em> link on that page confirms it works. Nothing else needs changing, and PDFs
        downloaded afterwards include the pages and the marks.</p>
        <p>A single mark can also be left off a page when its phrase cannot be found in the
        document's text, for example in a scanned page that has no text. A comment left off this
        way is listed in the summary.</p>
    </div>
</details>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>Word files or online text do not open as PDFs at all</summary>
    <div>
        <ul>
            <li>A document converter must be enabled in Moodle (<strong>Site administration &gt; Plugins &gt; Document converters</strong>) and pass its own test.</li>
            <li>For online text, <em>Render online text as PDF</em> must also be on. Without it, online text shows inline with a reduced toolbar. That is expected.</li>
            <li>After the converter comes back, <strong>Retry conversion</strong> clears the failed attempt. There is no need to wait.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</details>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>Annotations did not save</summary>
    <div>
        <p>Look at the save status in the header. <em>Offline — saved locally</em> means the
        connection dropped: the marks are kept in the browser and sent when it returns. If the page
        was reloaded first, choose <strong>Restore</strong> when the grader offers the unsaved
        changes. An expired login has the same effect; log in again in another tab.</p>
    </div>
</details>

<h4>Grades and penalties</h4>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>A late submission has no penalty</summary>
    <div>
        <ul>
            <li><em>Apply late penalties</em> must be ticked in the activity's settings. New activities start with it off.</li>
            <li>Penalty rules must exist for the site, the course or the activity in Moodle's grade penalty settings.</li>
            <li>The activity needs a due date. A quiz with only a closing date is never late.</li>
            <li>The student may have an extension or an override: check <strong>Dates &amp; extensions</strong>.</li>
            <li>On a quiz, the first real attempt decides. If it was on time, later attempts are not penalised.</li>
            <li>On a forum graded by post ratings, penalties apply only when the ratings are points (not a scale) and the <em>Aggregate type</em> is average or sum. Count, maximum and minimum never take a penalty.</li>
            <li>For an assignment with Moodle's own <em>Apply penalties</em> on, while Assignment is still a supported module for Moodle's grade penalties, Moodle applies the penalty and the Unified Grader stands back.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</details>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>The penalty is for more days than the student was late</summary>
    <div>
        <p>Each day that has started counts. A submission 1 day and 23 hours late is charged for
        2 days. The banner shows the exact lateness; the badge shows the days charged.</p>
    </div>
</details>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>The student cannot see a grade that shows as posted</summary>
    <div>
        <ul>
            <li>With Friction Feedback on, the mark stays hidden until the student finishes the walk, or until the fail-safe releases it.</li>
            <li>On a quiz, posting one student shows the grade in the gradebook and in the Unified Grader feedback, but the quiz's own review page still follows its review options.</li>
            <li>Check the eye beside the student in the student list: a class can be partly posted.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</details>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>There is no post-grades control on a quiz</summary>
    <div>
        <p><em>Enable post grades for quizzes</em> is off (<a href="#settings-grading">Grading settings</a>).
        Quiz marks are then shown according to the quiz review options only.</p>
    </div>
</details>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>A typed grade does not stay when a rubric is used</summary>
    <div>
        <p><em>Allow manual grade override</em> is off, so the grade always comes from the rubric or
        marking guide. Switch it on under <a href="#settings-grading">Grading settings</a> if teachers should be able to adjust it.</p>
    </div>
</details>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>Rubric scores cannot be saved: the grade is locked or overridden</summary>
    <div>
        <p>The student's grade is locked or overridden in the gradebook. Unlock it there, or type
        <code>--</code> in the grade box and save to release an override, then mark again.</p>
    </div>
</details>

<h4>Integrity and proctoring</h4>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>No plagiarism card appears</summary>
    <div>
        <p>Plagiarism plugins must be enabled on the site and set up for the activity, and the
        plugin must have returned a result for that file or text. The top of the
        <a href="#settings-integrity">Academic integrity</a> settings page says whether they are enabled.</p>
    </div>
</details>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>No proctoring marker or card on a proctored quiz</summary>
    <div>
        <ul>
            <li>The service must be ticked under <em>Proctoring services to show</em>.</li>
            <li>The viewer needs <code>local/unifiedgrader:viewproctoring</code>.</li>
            <li>The service's Moodle plugin must be installed and in use for that quiz. For SMOWL, the course needs the SMOWL block and the quiz must be switched on in the SMOWL panel; otherwise the card says <em>SMOWL is not active on this quiz</em>.</li>
            <li><em>Awaiting review</em> is not a fault: the service has not finished. Use the refresh button later.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</details>

<h4>BigBlueButton</h4>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>Activity Points are empty or say the summary has not been received</summary>
    <div>
        <p>Moodle's BigBlueButton setting <em>Register live sessions</em> is off, or the server is
        not keeping events (see <a href="#plugin-advgrd">BigBlueButton setup</a>). Summaries are
        sent only for sessions that start after both are on. For existing recordings use
        <strong>Refresh attendance</strong>.</p>
    </div>
</details>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>The recording is blank</summary>
    <div>
        <p>Try <strong>Open in new tab</strong>. If that fails too, the recording is not published
        yet, or the network blocks the server that hosts it. Check the activity's own list of recordings.</p>
    </div>
</details>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>Every session is listed for a student who attended only some</summary>
    <div>
        <p>The grader could not match the student's attendance to the recordings, and says so under
        the session pills. Press <strong>Refresh attendance</strong> to read attendance from each recording.</p>
    </div>
</details>

<h4>Comment library</h4>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>Comments from one course do not appear in another</summary>
    <div>
        <p>Comments are filed under a course code taken from the course short name. If the
        <a href="#settings-library">course code regex</a> is empty or does not match, each course
        has its own code. Teachers can move comments in <em>Organise my comment library</em>;
        managers can do so for anyone in <em>Moderate comment libraries</em>.</p>
    </div>
</details>

<p class="local-unifiedgrader-help-fine">Still stuck? Contact your site administrator, or report
the problem to the plugin's maintainers with the Moodle version, the plugin release shown at the
top of this page, and what you see on screen.</p>
</section>
